{"name":"Bear Rug","hex":"#5a4943","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bear","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large, generally omnivorous mammal (a few species are purely carnivorous or herbivorous) of the family Ursidae; having shaggy fur, a very small tail, and flat feet.\n The meat of this animal.","The meat of this animal."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To endeavour to depress the price of, or prices in."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bear"},{"term":"rug","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Roviana."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A partial covering for a floor. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A (usually thick) piece of fabric used for warmth (especially on a bed); a blanket."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rug"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bear","blocks":[{"text":"Bears are carnivoran mammals of the family Ursidae. They are classified as caniforms within the suborder Caniformia. Although only eight species of bears are extant, they are widespread, appearing in a wide variety of habitats throughout most of the Northern Hemisphere and partially in the Southern Hemisphere. Bears are found on the continents of North America, South America, and Eurasia. Common characteristics of modern bears include large bodies with stocky legs, long snouts, small rounded ears, shaggy hair, plantigrade paws with five nonretractile claws, and short tails."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Ours_brun_parcanimalierpyrenees_1.jpg/330px-Ours_brun_parcanimalierpyrenees_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear"},{"title":"Carpet","blocks":[{"text":"A carpet or rug is a textile floor covering that typically consists of an upper layer of pile attached to a backing. In Europe, the pile was traditionally made of wool, but since the 20th century, synthetic fibres such as polypropylene, nylon, and polyester have been used as less expensive alternatives. The pile often consists of twisted tufts that are heat-treated to maintain their structure."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Wollteppich_1.jpg/330px-Wollteppich_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carpet"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Ursidae_distribution.png/500px-Ursidae_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Ursidae_distribution.png/1280px-Ursidae_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Ursidae_distribution.png/500px-Ursidae_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUrsidae_distribution.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Plithocyon_armagnacensis.JPG/500px-Plithocyon_armagnacensis.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Plithocyon_armagnacensis.JPG/500px-Plithocyon_armagnacensis.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Plithocyon armagnacensis skull, a member of the extinct subfamily Hemicyoninae from the Miocene","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APlithocyon_armagnacensis.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Arctotherium.jpg/500px-Arctotherium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Arctotherium.jpg/1280px-Arctotherium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm